<title>CHINA: China rubber imports seen unchanged from last year.</title>
<headline>China rubber imports seen unchanged from last year.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's rubber imports for 1997 are seen basically unchanged from last year despite stockpiles of about 200,000 tonnes from last year, the China Business Daily said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Imports in 1996 were excessive and estimates are that about 200,000 tonnes of material will spill over for use this year,&quot; the newspaper said.</p>
<p>But imports for 1997 would not be less than last year, it said, adding that China's tyre production was seen rising by six percent this year to 70.3 million tyres.</p>
<p>China imported 450,000 tonnes of natural rubber and 300,000 tonnes of synthetic rubber last year, official reports have said.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
